   "Branch feat/batch-14-item-1-{slug} will be created before any file write."

## Recommended Batch 14 — pick ONE primary direction:

### Direction A — E-commerce Phase 1 (single-item T3 batch, ~50-60K)
Establishes the storefront order pipeline. New Order + EcommerceOrder entities, storefront
router (browse → cart → checkout), inventory hold on order placement, link to Purchase Order
when stock falls below reorder point.

Files to touch (proposed — re-verify at pre-flight):
- packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma — Order, EcommerceOrder, OrderItem models + indexes.
- packages/db/prisma/migrations/{TS}_add_ecommerce_orders/migration.sql — manual SQL.
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/storefront.ts — NEW router (browse/cart/checkout/orderById).
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/root.ts — register storefront router.
- apps/web/src/__tests__/storefront.test.ts — NEW comprehensive test suite (~25+ tests).
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/ecommerce/orders/page.tsx — admin list.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/ecommerce/orders/[id]/page.tsx — admin detail.
- (Storefront-facing public pages can defer to Batch 15.)

### Direction B — Mobile WatermelonDB DTR Phase 1 (single-item T3+ batch, ~60-80K)
Offline DTR (Daily Time Record) sync for technicians on field calls. Establishes the mobile
sync foundation. Pair with backend sync endpoints. May overflow single Opus 4.7 session
— consider Architect-Execute split (§4 memory-governance.md).

### Direction C — Small carry-forward bundle (2 items, ~20-30K combined)
- Item 1: Reverse JE accounting hardening — wrap accounting.reverse in db.$transaction;
  add 3-4 tests for partial-failure rollback. T1 ~5-10K.
- Item 2: AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true defaults in .env.staging / .env.prod templates +
  scripts/sync-credentials-to-env.sh update. T1 ~5K, config-only.
- Item 3 (optional): Quotation builder Phase 3 — column reordering UI + save/load named
  markup-column templates. T2 ~15-20K.

## Trigger
Open Claude Code in this folder. Say "start Phase 8 Batch 14" — agent will read STATE.md
first, run the 8-point pre-flight (now including mock-payload-completeness check from
Batch 13), then emit BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL with explicit branch-creation line items per
Rule 23. Pick Direction A, B, or C at the proposal confirmation stage.
